Find position (in grapheme units) of first occurrence of a string

&reftitle.changelog;





    &Version;
    &Description;



   &intl.changelog.grapheme.locale;


    7.1.0

     Support for negative offsets has been added.

  &reftitle.examples;

   grapheme_strpos example


<?php

$char_a_ring_nfd = "a\xCC\x8A";  // 'LATIN SMALL LETTER A WITH RING ABOVE' (U+00E5) normalization form "D"
$char_o_diaeresis_nfd = "o\xCC\x88"; // 'LATIN SMALL LETTER O WITH DIAERESIS' (U+00F6) normalization form "D"

print grapheme_strpos( $char_a_ring_nfd . $char_a_ring_nfd . $char_o_diaeresis_nfd, $char_o_diaeresis_nfd);

?>



  &example.outputs;


2



   Using the ks-identic locale key to distinguish variation selectors

    By default, Unicode variation selectors (U+FE0E text, U+FE0F emoji) are ignored
    during comparison. Using the ks-identic locale extension key
    enables identical-level collation, which treats them as distinct characters.



     The locale parameter is available since PHP 8.5.0.




<?php

$textStyle  = "\u{263A}\u{FE0E}"; // U+263A + U+FE0E (text presentation selector)
$emojiStyle = "\u{263A}\u{FE0F}"; // U+263A + U+FE0F (emoji presentation selector)

// Default locale: variation selectors are ignored, so the needle is found at position 0.
var_dump(grapheme_strpos($textStyle, $emojiStyle));

// With ks-identic: variation selectors are significant, so no match is found.
var_dump(grapheme_strpos($textStyle, $emojiStyle, 0, 'en_US-u-ks-identic'));

?>


